1
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,120
(This series is a fictional work created
for entertainment purposes.)

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,240
(The characters, events, locations, organizations
agencies, as well as religions, beliefs)

3
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,360
(and symbols appearing in this story
are presented for storytelling purposes only.)

4
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:10,160
(No intention is made to reference, imply, criticize)

5
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:10,960
(or allude to any individual,
organization or religious group)

6
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,400
Hey

7
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:16,520
(Chat)

8
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:24,400
I thought I wouldn't be able to live without you

9
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:28,160
But look at me now

10
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:29,840
I'm shining

11
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:31,640
On nights when the sky turns against me

12
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:34,680
When the rain falls inside my heart

13
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:35,720
I play the same old songs

14
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,920
That we used to listen to together

15
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,800
Your picture is still right there

16
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:41,560
But I'm not crying anymore

17
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:42,600
I used to want you so badly

18
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:44,000
Now I'm beginning to understand

19
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:46,920
That love comes and go

20
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,880
I thought my whole world had to fall apart

21
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:49,680
But in the end

22
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:53,520
It was just my heart learning how to move on

23
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:57,120
I used to say "Can't live without you"

24
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,760
But today, I can proudly say, I'm cool

25
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:00,960
I’m looking so good

26
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:03,680
Damn I don’t even try to do

27
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:07,240
Good without you, I’m doing fine

28
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:09,600
Me without you, I can manage

29
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:12,000
Already told you, don’t come back, don’t show your face

30
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:13,960
I can still smile, easy and free

31
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:35,240
Damn it!

32
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:07,880
Hey!

33
00:02:08,479 --> 00:02:09,360
Hey!

34
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:11,880
Anyone here?

35
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:39,560
Hello.

36
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:42,240
Chat, an insider says Ms. Nichakorn

37
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:43,960
will be attending the meeting this morning too.

38
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:44,920
What meeting?

39
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,079
No need to ask.

40
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:47,920
Get dressed and come out right away!

41
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:50,120
Yeah, alright.

42
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:04,360
Here we go.

43
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:15,160
What to do?

44
00:03:16,079 --> 00:03:17,880
Ugh, why does everyone keep calling?

45
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:30,480
Prepare your documents.

46
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:32,760
He hasn’t picked up yet.

47
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,360
Hello? Hello, Chat?

48
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:38,040
Where are you?

49
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:40,240
I'll be there in five minutes.

50
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:43,800
Huh? Five more minutes?

51
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:46,960
Oh no, by then Ms. Nichakorn will

52
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:48,280
probably have arrived already.

53
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:50,720
Please hurry up and come.

54
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:51,880
What to do?

55
00:03:52,320 --> 00:03:54,200
The other team is here.

56
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:02,840
Just stay still.

57
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:33,320
Sorry! Excuse me!

58
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:37,480
Could you help me with something?

59
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:40,400
If Ms. Nichakorn is about to reach the elevator,

60
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:42,080
can you please call me?

61
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:02,680
Hello, Ms. Nichakorn.

62
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:15,640
The target is heading straight for the elevator.

63
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:18,960
Okay.

64
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,480
What wrong with the elevator? Why is it so slow?

65
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,920
Send someone to examine it.

66
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Yes, ma'am.

67
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:06,200
Ms. Dao.

68
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:08,520
Could you please go up and check

69
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:10,360
why the elevator still hasn't come down?

70
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:11,880
Ms. Nichakorn has been waiting for a long time.

71
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:13,520
Oh. Umm...

72
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,120
Okay. Sure.

73
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:16,760
Thank you.

74
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:20,280
What to do?

75
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:28,760
Hey, brother! Go over there!

76
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,120
Just go!

77
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:35,480
I asked Dao to go check.

78
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:49,760
Please hold on to it for a bit!

79
00:06:57,159 --> 00:06:58,280
Hey, Nueng.

80
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:00,280
Please quickly go in, Chat.

81
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:01,880
Did you help me?

82
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:06,760
Please head in quickly, everyone is waiting for you.

83
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:08,120
Mmm.

84
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:09,880
Please wait, Chat.

85
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:27,760
All done.

86
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,040
I'll enter the room first.

87
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,080
Okay.

88
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:43,240
It's been more than five minutes.

89
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:44,360
He's here.

90
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:45,520
He's here.

91
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,680
You made it in time!

92
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:58,760
Almost didn't make it.

93
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:10,520
Nueng, where did you go?

94
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:12,160
I went to the restroom.

95
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:15,160
I hope what you say is actually true.

96
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:18,680
How did it go last night?

97
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:20,600
You're the one who dates randomly.

98
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:21,880
Geez.

99
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:23,440
She's here.

100
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,760
Hello.

101
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:29,920
Hello.

102
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,120
Please take a seat.

103
00:08:35,039 --> 00:08:36,120
Hello everyone.

104
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:37,960
The reason I’ve called you all to an urgent meeting today

105
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:40,799
is that I have an important announcement to make.

106
00:08:41,919 --> 00:08:43,880
It may be a major change for us,

107
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:48,560
because a new department head will be joining

108
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:52,400
to help oversee and support both Team A and Team B.

109
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:55,680
He is a product specialist

110
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:57,400
from Vega Lab Korea,

111
00:08:57,480 --> 00:09:00,080
which is already a partner of all of ours.

112
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:54,360
Please welcome Mr. Choi Seungwoo,

113
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:56,960
our new Head of Product.

114
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,360
Hello everyone.

115
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,920
I’m Choi Seungwoo.

116
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:09,720
Nice to meet you all.

117
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:14,760
Our product development group has two teams.

118
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:16,320
Team A

119
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:18,200
is led by Ms. Mira,

120
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:20,720
with Mr. Tommy, Ms. Plai, and Mr. Nueng.

121
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:26,760
Team B has Mr. June, Ms. Ja, Mr. Pek,

122
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:29,120
and the team leader is Mr. Chat.

123
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:35,880
Chat.

124
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:37,600
Hmm?

125
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:48,400
Hello.

126
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,760
Nice to meet you all.

127
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:55,640
I hope

128
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:59,120
we'll work well together.

129
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:03,840
Of course.

130
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:10,480
I studied the work

131
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:13,160
and products you’ve all developed carefully.

132
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:16,480
Before we start working in earnest,

133
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:18,840
I’d like to look at

134
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:21,320
Team B’s work first.

135
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:34,800
Just Team B?

136
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:36,720
Yes, just Team B.

137
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:39,400
Team B Leader...

138
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,360
Please be prepared.

139
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:45,400
Yes.

140
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:58,520
Drinks are here.

141
00:11:58,600 --> 00:11:59,800
Here you go.

142
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:00,760
Lovely.

143
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:02,160
It’s delicious today, give it a try.

144
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:08,400
The type of noodles little June wanted,

145
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:10,240
here it is.

146
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:14,280
It looks delicious!

147
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:16,800
Oh, let me ask you something.

148
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:19,160
People are gossiping that

149
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:21,320
the new manager from Korea

150
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:24,600
is handsome and totally hot. Is it true?

151
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:27,400
Sister, true or not, just look at Tommy,

152
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:29,000
still raving about him.

153
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:32,960
I’ll probably have to stop loving Nueng

154
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:35,720
and date Mr. Seungwoo instead.

155
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:39,640
What a man, handsome like he stepped out of a drama.

156
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:44,080
This time I’ll finally be the real female lead.

157
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:48,760
So delusional, right?

158
00:12:49,160 --> 00:12:50,640
Last night

159
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:52,520
I was watching a Korean drama,

160
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:54,080
and there was this one character

161
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:56,080
who was so delusional.

162
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:58,480
If I could step through the screen,

163
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:01,120
I’d yank her hair and slap them once or twice

164
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:02,840
so they'd stop fantasizing.

165
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:09,400
Pity the ones who want to curse but don’t dare.

166
00:13:09,920 --> 00:13:11,560
They can barely move

167
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:13,640
because they’re on conduct probation.

168
00:13:13,720 --> 00:13:16,320
Oh, nearly getting fired too,

169
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:19,400
so they’d better know their place.

170
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:21,480
If you’re going to talk like that, then settle this once and for all.

171
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:23,360
Fine, come on, come!

172
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:26,120
Do you have some issues?

173
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:27,080
So what?

174
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:28,520
Huh?

175
00:13:28,920 --> 00:13:29,960
You keep taking jabs.

176
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,240
If you have free time,

177
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:34,040
go dye your hair,

178
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:36,880
so it won’t be half black, half gray.

179
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:39,440
But you started it, sis.

180
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:40,920
Once doesn’t count.

181
00:13:44,640 --> 00:13:47,160
This is called fashion, dear.

182
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:48,920
Someone with no taste like you

183
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,120
has the nerve to criticize others.

184
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:55,080
Spend your time on a hair treatment.

185
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:57,000
All you do is spray,

186
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:59,520
I can’t tell whether it’s your hair or your head that’s hard.

187
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:04,680
Um, Team A and Team B usually have conflicts quite often,

188
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:06,200
but the company views

189
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:08,160
the problems arising from competition

190
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:09,480
as pushing both teams

191
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:11,880
to produce their best work.

192
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:25,080
That’s enough!

193
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:27,080
This is a canteen.

194
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:28,840
If you want to fight, go fight somewhere else!

195
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:31,160
Don’t back down, Tommy.

196
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:32,800
If someone’s picking a fight,

197
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:35,240
wherever it is, hit them back.

198
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:37,440
Right, we're not selling anything anymore!

199
00:14:37,520 --> 00:14:38,640
June, don’t back down!

200
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:39,360
Bring it on!

201
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:40,080
Get them!

202
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:40,760
Come then!

203
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:42,240
Come at me!

204
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:43,720
Enough, sis!

205
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:45,680
Stop, stop, sis, stop!

206
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:46,720
Every time there's a fight,

207
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:48,400
I’m the one who ends up cleaning up!

208
00:14:52,040 --> 00:14:53,560
Enough fun.

209
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:05,040
I think

210
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:06,120
it’s better to give Team B

211
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:08,880
time to prepare their presentation for the new manager.

212
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:11,200
Your results are in the negative,

213
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:13,480
so you’ll probably be watched closely.

214
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:18,560
Present well,

215
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:29,440
and be careful.

216
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:31,960
Three months

217
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:39,360
will become just one.

218
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:55,920
Come on.

219
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,080
Don’t buy drinks from this shop.

220
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:58,480
It’s okay, sis.

221
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:01,960
Chat.

222
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:10,720
Chat.

223
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:13,960
What's with you today?

224
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:16,600
Why did you let team A mess with us?

225
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:21,160
Last night I caught

226
00:16:21,240 --> 00:16:22,680
Jeno sleeping with someone.

227
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:23,600
Huh?

228
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:25,120
Mmm.

229
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:28,000
So I went to a pub,

230
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:30,000
I planned to get drunk

231
00:16:30,760 --> 00:16:32,080
but I messed up and slept with someone.

232
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:34,640
Isn't it fine?

233
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:36,280
Your boyfriend did it.

234
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,560
So can you!

235
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:38,520
Isn't it fabulous?

236
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:39,760
How is it fabulous?

237
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:42,240
The one I slept with was

238
00:16:44,400 --> 00:16:45,320
Mr. Choi Seungwoo.

239
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:48,040
Hey!

240
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:49,240
Mmm.

241
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:52,080
I don't know if I should be jealous of you or pity you.

242
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:54,120
Why does bad luck keep happening to you?

243
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:55,520
But

244
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:57,560
it’s a stroke of incredible good fortune.

245
00:16:57,640 --> 00:16:59,400
He's insanely handsome!

246
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:03,920
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

247
00:17:05,520 --> 00:17:07,880
Does this mean you're on the fast track

248
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:09,880
to having your superior as your boyfriend?

249
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:11,680
What fast track are you talking about?

250
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:14,119
I don't know if he remembers me.

251
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,599
I hope he doesn't remember.

252
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:19,240
What?

253
00:17:19,319 --> 00:17:20,400
Was it mind-blowing?

254
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:21,359
Come on!

255
00:17:25,119 --> 00:17:26,319
Why is it that your team

256
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,360
hasn’t had any top-form results lately?

257
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:37,880
Can anyone answer me?

258
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:40,440
The latest failure was my fault.

259
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:42,280
I didn’t research the competitor’s information

260
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:43,040
well enough beforehand.

261
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:48,680
Umm...

262
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:51,800
My packaging design

263
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:53,720
also still isn’t quite up to there yet.

264
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:57,320
I have tried to come up with the best formula possible,

265
00:17:57,960 --> 00:18:00,440
but it isn’t any different from the competitors on the market.

266
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:04,120
What about you?

267
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:08,880
You.

268
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:12,480
Mr. Chat, leader of team B.

269
00:18:14,280 --> 00:18:15,120
Mr. Chat.

270
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,280
Why do you think it is?

271
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:19,880
Well, our team is about to develop...

272
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:21,240
I didn’t ask

273
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,200
what you’re working on.

274
00:18:23,280 --> 00:18:24,280
I asked why.

275
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:26,160
Why?

276
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:36,680
I’ll need to speak with Team B’s leader

277
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:38,600
privately.

278
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:47,840
Ugh, what's going on?

279
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:49,120
It's been a while already.

280
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:50,040
True.

281
00:18:50,120 --> 00:18:51,360
Go, go.

282
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:53,120
Fah.

283
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:55,560
Why is this new boss so brutal?

284
00:18:57,040 --> 00:18:58,440
I showed him around the company for quite a while,

285
00:18:58,520 --> 00:19:00,040
and he didn't seem harsh.

286
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:01,240
I'm confused too.

287
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:03,360
Oh, you don't know, sisters.

288
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:05,280
When it comes to work,

289
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:07,200
Korean people take it very seriously.

290
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:09,640
Isn't this too serious?

291
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:11,520
How is Chat doing?

292
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:12,320
Yeah.

293
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:13,920
Probably got chewed out.

294
00:19:18,040 --> 00:19:19,680
You lot watch out too.

295
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:22,160
Be careful, or you'll be the next one to get torn to shreds.

296
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:25,160
You team A better be careful too.

297
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:26,680
Thanks for the warning,

298
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:28,320
but you lot should warn yourselves instead.

299
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:30,160
Team A is safe.

300
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:38,120
Let's go.

301
00:19:39,760 --> 00:19:41,200
Sister, look.

302
00:19:52,680 --> 00:19:53,800
I admit it,

303
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:56,800
Team B's performance has had some problems lately,

304
00:20:00,080 --> 00:20:02,480
but everyone is capable.

305
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:23,360
You still can't take it out?

306
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,840
Is it fun teasing me like this?

307
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:28,320
If it was last night,

308
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:29,960
yes.

309
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:34,160
The sound handcuffs make when they clink together

310
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:36,000
is pretty funny.

311
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:41,520
Keep your jokes to yourself.

312
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:43,240
Give me the key.

313
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:48,600
This?

314
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:52,480
Then

315
00:20:53,760 --> 00:20:54,840
take it back by yourself.

316
00:20:58,160 --> 00:20:59,680
Why are you doing this?

317
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:02,560
It seems like you're having fun

318
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,960
just like last night.

319
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:09,800
Stop talking about last night.

320
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:12,160
It will never happen again.

321
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:15,400
And

322
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:17,680
I’ll be waiting to see

323
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:22,440
who it is that causes this

324
00:21:24,040 --> 00:21:24,880
to happen again.

325
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:33,000
Here are your coffees.

326
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:39,080
Chat already went home.

327
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:40,480
He won't be drinking coffee with you.

328
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:45,160
That's fine.

329
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:47,760
I can drink two cups of coffee.

330
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:53,560
Can you stop acting like this?

331
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:56,320
Don't you know that what you're doing

332
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:58,760
may get Chat in trouble.

333
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:03,960
How does this affect you?

334
00:22:04,040 --> 00:22:06,040
The fact that you’re getting involved with Chat like this,

335
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:09,160
if your team finds out,

336
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,960
they’re definitely going to be unhappy.

337
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:14,960
And if your team uses this to cause trouble for Chat,

338
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:17,120
what are you going to do?

339
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:20,440
I'm also worried about him.

340
00:22:20,520 --> 00:22:23,280
And I'll never let him get in trouble, you know?

341
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:25,680
Your Thai tea with less sugar is ready.

342
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:35,320
Stop looking at me in such a negative light.

343
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:43,120
Drink something sweet

344
00:22:43,520 --> 00:22:44,760
so your mood will get better.

345
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:52,160
I don't want it.

346
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:01,480
You don't believe me?

347
00:23:09,040 --> 00:23:09,960
Here.

348
00:23:10,560 --> 00:23:12,360
They say sugar actually helps

349
00:23:12,440 --> 00:23:13,840
improve your mood, you know.

350
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:17,640
Try it.

351
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:21,040
Just a little.

352
00:23:34,760 --> 00:23:35,720
Thank you.

353
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:46,560
(Mr. Peck)

354
00:24:58,520 --> 00:24:59,600
Teerach.

355
00:25:01,680 --> 00:25:02,520
Teerach.

356
00:25:02,600 --> 00:25:03,800
Teerach, stop.

357
00:25:04,960 --> 00:25:06,560
Your mom came up to call you,

358
00:25:06,640 --> 00:25:07,960
there must be something urgent.

359
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:09,960
You should go see her first.

360
00:25:44,120 --> 00:25:45,120
Still not going down?

361
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:47,320
Why do I have to go down too?

362
00:25:47,400 --> 00:25:49,200
This morning you didn’t go to congratulate

363
00:25:49,280 --> 00:25:50,640
your younger brother at the company either.

364
00:25:50,720 --> 00:25:52,040
And now you’re not going down too?

365
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:54,120
Do I have to care about him?

366
00:25:56,600 --> 00:25:58,200
He's your younger brother.

367
00:26:37,320 --> 00:26:38,120
Hello.

368
00:26:39,560 --> 00:26:40,480
Hello.

369
00:26:41,320 --> 00:26:43,360
Hurry up and eat, so we can get this over with.

370
00:26:45,800 --> 00:26:48,520
How was your first day at work?

371
00:26:49,080 --> 00:26:50,680
Is there anything weighing on your mind?

372
00:26:51,680 --> 00:26:54,400
No. Everything is very well organized.

373
00:26:57,520 --> 00:27:00,000
No need to bring anyone else in to handle the management.

374
00:27:02,680 --> 00:27:05,200
Your brother just wanted to try working in Thailand.

375
00:27:08,760 --> 00:27:09,600
Why?

376
00:27:10,640 --> 00:27:13,240
Does your Korean father not trust you anymore?

377
00:27:14,160 --> 00:27:15,480
Is that why you're here?

378
00:27:17,760 --> 00:27:19,720
I just want some new experience.

379
00:27:19,800 --> 00:27:21,920
If you really want a new experience,

380
00:27:23,040 --> 00:27:24,840
try acting like a regular employee

381
00:27:25,800 --> 00:27:27,600
and stop telling everyone you're mom's son.

382
00:27:28,120 --> 00:27:30,120
That's the real new experience.

383
00:27:33,600 --> 00:27:35,160
I never told anyone

384
00:27:35,720 --> 00:27:36,960
that I'm our mom's son.

385
00:27:37,840 --> 00:27:38,720
Then

386
00:27:39,400 --> 00:27:40,840
please don't tell anyone, mom.

387
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:42,880
Is that a good idea?

388
00:27:42,960 --> 00:27:44,240
That's good.

389
00:27:45,680 --> 00:27:48,320
That way we can prove once and for all whether this son of yours

390
00:27:49,120 --> 00:27:50,800
is good because of himself,

391
00:27:50,880 --> 00:27:52,080
or because of someone else.

392
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:24,920
Why do you hate your own younger brother that much, Teerach?

393
00:28:33,600 --> 00:28:35,600
When we were kids, we had to fight over Mom.

394
00:28:38,400 --> 00:28:39,840
When he was sick,

395
00:28:40,440 --> 00:28:42,560
Mom had to go to Korea to take care of him,

396
00:28:44,440 --> 00:28:46,600
and she left me to grow up all alone here.

397
00:28:49,200 --> 00:28:50,560
When Mom came back,

398
00:28:54,080 --> 00:28:55,480
he followed her here too.

399
00:29:02,200 --> 00:29:03,920
You're acting like this

400
00:29:04,720 --> 00:29:07,240
because you're afraid of losing your mom again, right?

401
00:29:17,960 --> 00:29:19,040
Hey, doc.

402
00:29:19,600 --> 00:29:21,560
Are you analyzing the issues in my heart?

403
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:25,440
That's not it.

404
00:29:27,840 --> 00:29:30,320
I just don't want you to drown in your own suffering.

405
00:29:33,440 --> 00:29:35,080
I'm used to living with him.

406
00:29:35,600 --> 00:29:36,800
You don't have to worry.

407
00:29:41,840 --> 00:29:44,320
I will not let everything that belongs to me be taken away.

408
00:30:35,360 --> 00:30:37,720
Why didn't you answer my calls?

409
00:30:41,160 --> 00:30:43,320
I called you all night, you know?

410
00:30:47,320 --> 00:30:48,720
I have nothing to say.

411
00:30:49,160 --> 00:30:50,840
I know I was wrong.

412
00:30:51,640 --> 00:30:53,760
I’m not going to make any excuses.

413
00:30:54,920 --> 00:30:56,520
Chat, can we...

414
00:30:57,560 --> 00:30:58,800
Let's break up.

415
00:31:04,080 --> 00:31:05,320
Are you serious?

416
00:31:06,720 --> 00:31:07,680
Mmm.

417
00:31:45,040 --> 00:31:47,200
You said you wouldn't abandon me.

418
00:31:53,400 --> 00:31:55,640
You can make me do anything for you.

419
00:31:59,840 --> 00:32:01,640
But please don't abandon me.

420
00:32:27,960 --> 00:32:29,640
It's time you grow up, Jeno.

421
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:40,200
So, I can no longer stay here, right?

422
00:32:45,960 --> 00:32:47,400
No matter what happens,

423
00:32:47,480 --> 00:32:49,200
I would never abandon you.

424
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:52,720
You've said it!

425
00:32:53,360 --> 00:32:54,880
If you abandoned me,

426
00:32:55,240 --> 00:32:56,880
I would have no place to go.

427
00:33:08,680 --> 00:33:10,440
Then you can stay here for now.

428
00:33:14,120 --> 00:33:15,680
The room is still vacant anyway.

429
00:33:18,640 --> 00:33:20,760
You can move out whenever you’re ready.

430
00:33:30,080 --> 00:33:31,960
This is as much as I can keep my promise.

431
00:34:18,920 --> 00:34:20,800
I'm sorry.

432
00:34:37,080 --> 00:34:39,000
Because one single mistake

433
00:34:39,520 --> 00:34:41,280
will cause everything to fall apart.

434
00:34:51,199 --> 00:34:52,239
What’s that mark?

435
00:34:54,320 --> 00:34:55,719
Let's break up.

436
00:34:55,800 --> 00:34:56,960
Chat!

437
00:34:57,040 --> 00:34:58,280
Chat!

438
00:34:58,360 --> 00:35:00,400
You said you wouldn't abandon me.

439
00:35:12,320 --> 00:35:13,480
Work-wise,

440
00:35:13,560 --> 00:35:15,160
we might be rivals,

441
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:16,560
but

442
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:19,080
when it comes to personal matters, I...

443
00:35:25,320 --> 00:35:26,720
I already told you...

444
00:35:28,840 --> 00:35:29,920
And I’ll be waiting to see

445
00:35:30,400 --> 00:35:33,760
who it is that causes this

446
00:35:34,920 --> 00:35:36,080
to happen again.

447
00:35:53,320 --> 00:35:55,040
How long are you going to sit there spaced out?

448
00:35:57,720 --> 00:35:59,160
So you broke up with your boyfriend,

449
00:35:59,240 --> 00:36:00,720
it’s not like the world ended, right?

450
00:36:04,440 --> 00:36:06,120
What would you understand?

451
00:36:08,040 --> 00:36:09,600
You've never been in a relationship.

452
00:36:10,120 --> 00:36:11,280
You really loved him,

453
00:36:12,040 --> 00:36:13,160
but you cheated on him,

454
00:36:13,600 --> 00:36:14,520
huh?

455
00:36:18,880 --> 00:36:20,280
I just made a mistake.

456
00:36:21,560 --> 00:36:22,920
You're my friend, okay?

457
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:25,400
Shouldn’t you be helping me figure out how to win Chat back?

458
00:36:37,200 --> 00:36:38,600
(ROV game competition. First-place prize money 1,000,000 baht)

459
00:36:38,680 --> 00:36:39,720
See this?

460
00:36:40,360 --> 00:36:41,440
If you can win,

461
00:36:42,240 --> 00:36:44,560
he’ll be able to see that you’re taking life more seriously.

462
00:36:53,120 --> 00:36:54,720
But it's not easy.

463
00:36:54,800 --> 00:36:56,280
If you win,

464
00:36:57,880 --> 00:36:59,600
Chat will get a better boyfriend.

465
00:37:00,200 --> 00:37:02,440
But if he doesn't want you back at all,

466
00:37:04,280 --> 00:37:06,880
at least you can be proud of yourself.

467
00:37:11,920 --> 00:37:14,720
(ROV game competition. First-place prize money 1,000,000 baht)

468
00:37:27,960 --> 00:37:28,800
Hey.

469
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:30,760
Spill the tea.

470
00:37:31,560 --> 00:37:33,440
You should’ve seen Mr. Chat’s face,

471
00:37:33,520 --> 00:37:34,600
listen.

472
00:37:34,680 --> 00:37:35,720
When Mr. Chat

473
00:37:35,800 --> 00:37:38,320
got called into the room by the Korean boss,

474
00:37:38,400 --> 00:37:39,960
you see, he came out

475
00:37:40,040 --> 00:37:42,120
looking pale as boiled chicken.

476
00:37:43,040 --> 00:37:45,040
Well, he got called one-on-one.

477
00:37:45,120 --> 00:37:46,240
He probably got scolded nonstop,

478
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:48,040
in Thai, Korean, and English.

479
00:37:48,120 --> 00:37:50,520
Oh, if it were just a scolding that’d be fine,

480
00:37:50,600 --> 00:37:53,440
because Mr. Chat is probably used to getting scolded by now.

481
00:37:53,520 --> 00:37:55,920
But what if he gets fired?

482
00:37:56,000 --> 00:37:56,920
Oh my god!

483
00:37:58,800 --> 00:38:00,120
Like the rumors say,

484
00:38:00,200 --> 00:38:02,160
they might get fired before the three months are up.

485
00:38:02,240 --> 00:38:03,280
These days,

486
00:38:03,360 --> 00:38:04,640
if you get fired suddenly,

487
00:38:04,720 --> 00:38:05,680
how are you going to make a living?

488
00:38:05,760 --> 00:38:06,760
Well,

489
00:38:07,240 --> 00:38:09,640
there’s glazed shiny pork!

490
00:38:09,720 --> 00:38:10,720
It’s amazing.

491
00:38:10,800 --> 00:38:12,560
One bite, one liter of water.

492
00:38:12,640 --> 00:38:14,760
Sometimes when they run out of pork, they make it with dog.

493
00:38:14,840 --> 00:38:16,840
Ew, I wouldn’t dare eat it.

494
00:38:16,920 --> 00:38:17,920
I don’t even know if it’s tasty.

495
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:18,840
It’s delicious!

496
00:38:18,920 --> 00:38:20,000
Some batches are sweet, some are sour.

497
00:38:20,920 --> 00:38:21,720
Stop joking around,

498
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:23,160
we’re talking about something serious here.

499
00:38:23,240 --> 00:38:25,200
Honestly though,

500
00:38:25,560 --> 00:38:28,280
Team B, what are they even doing competing with Team A?

501
00:38:28,360 --> 00:38:28,840
True.

502
00:38:28,920 --> 00:38:30,040
They can’t win anyway.

503
00:38:30,560 --> 00:38:33,320
Even the team names show the class difference so clearly.

504
00:38:33,400 --> 00:38:36,040
Hey, it’d be good if Team B left.

505
00:38:36,120 --> 00:38:38,000
Fewer employees means

506
00:38:38,080 --> 00:38:39,800
the company pays out less,

507
00:38:39,880 --> 00:38:41,560
and our bonuses go up.

508
00:38:41,640 --> 00:38:44,160
Team B staying is just dead weight on the company.

509
00:38:51,800 --> 00:38:52,720
Umm...

510
00:38:53,680 --> 00:38:55,720
Would you like more water, Nueng?

511
00:38:56,240 --> 00:38:58,080
No thanks, I'm full.

512
00:39:10,240 --> 00:39:12,720
Where are the documents?

513
00:39:14,160 --> 00:39:16,040
Not this.

514
00:39:23,800 --> 00:39:25,080
Did you enter the wrong room?

515
00:39:25,760 --> 00:39:26,680
No.

516
00:39:26,760 --> 00:39:28,480
I intentionally came to see you.

517
00:39:29,160 --> 00:39:30,200
What's up?

518
00:39:31,680 --> 00:39:33,960
Well, since this morning,

519
00:39:34,040 --> 00:39:35,800
I've seen you working so hard.

520
00:39:36,520 --> 00:39:39,000
So, I wanted to ask...

521
00:39:39,800 --> 00:39:41,480
Is there anything I can help you with?

522
00:39:43,520 --> 00:39:45,560
And what would I make you help with?

523
00:39:49,760 --> 00:39:50,800
Anything is fine.

524
00:39:51,400 --> 00:39:52,920
If you need my help,

525
00:39:53,000 --> 00:39:54,160
I can do anything.

526
00:39:57,040 --> 00:39:58,760
I'm the team leader,

527
00:39:58,840 --> 00:40:00,040
I can manage by myself.

528
00:40:01,720 --> 00:40:03,200
I know you're capable.

529
00:40:04,720 --> 00:40:05,960
But if you had someone else to lend a hand...

530
00:40:06,040 --> 00:40:07,920
Your job is

531
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:09,920
to support Team A in making their products

532
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:10,880
the best they can be,

533
00:40:11,640 --> 00:40:14,240
since our company releases new products every single month anyway.

534
00:40:16,280 --> 00:40:17,600
As for Team B,

535
00:40:17,680 --> 00:40:20,320
we'll always be Team A's scary rival.

536
00:40:23,120 --> 00:40:24,040
Therefore,

537
00:40:25,800 --> 00:40:27,000
you’ve made a mistake.

538
00:40:29,080 --> 00:40:30,280
But...

539
00:40:31,680 --> 00:40:33,040
Thank you.

540
00:40:38,760 --> 00:40:40,280
Because you're like this,

541
00:40:41,080 --> 00:40:42,520
so I...

542
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:50,280
Respect you.

543
00:40:51,120 --> 00:40:52,280
Mmm.

544
00:41:14,440 --> 00:41:16,480
I really admire your effort.

545
00:41:20,720 --> 00:41:21,840
Thanks

546
00:41:23,360 --> 00:41:24,600
for not getting in the way.

547
00:41:28,080 --> 00:41:29,440
It’s just not necessary.

548
00:41:30,480 --> 00:41:31,560
Because I already know that,

549
00:41:31,640 --> 00:41:33,520
Chat is never going to fall for your charms.

550
00:41:34,920 --> 00:41:35,760
Is that so?

551
00:41:36,440 --> 00:41:39,600
But usually, everyone falls for it.

552
00:41:43,200 --> 00:41:44,440
Do you think otherwise?

553
00:41:53,280 --> 00:41:54,760
Stop being so full of yourself.

554
00:41:55,760 --> 00:41:57,800
Do you think everyone is supposed to like you or something?

555
00:41:59,000 --> 00:42:01,280
It doesn't matter who likes me.

556
00:42:01,880 --> 00:42:02,960
Because I

557
00:42:03,600 --> 00:42:05,200
already have someone I like.

558
00:42:05,920 --> 00:42:07,720
It’s wrong to have feelings for someone

559
00:42:08,080 --> 00:42:09,360
who’s already taken, you know.

560
00:42:09,960 --> 00:42:11,280
Sis, spill the tea.

561
00:42:11,360 --> 00:42:12,360
Geez.

562
00:42:12,440 --> 00:42:13,840
Chat already broke up with his boyfriend.

563
00:42:13,920 --> 00:42:15,240
Huh? Already broke up?

564
00:42:15,320 --> 00:42:16,320
Break up.

565
00:42:16,400 --> 00:42:17,640
Don't go around telling others.

566
00:42:17,720 --> 00:42:18,920
Keep it to yourself.

567
00:42:20,600 --> 00:42:22,080
But it seems that this round,

568
